            <div xml:id="d405-a2">

                <pb facs="0738" n="638" xml:id="pg638"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    284.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract from Le Moniteur, April 8,
                    1880.]</seg></opener>
                <p>“The following extracts, in support of acts had by one of the most advanced
                    nations and the most rigidly attached to respect for its political rights, as
                    well as regards its own citizens as those of foreigners to whom it has given
                    shelter, leave no doubt as to the exteait of the powers of the state with regard
                    to this matter.</p>
                <p><quote rend="blockquote"><p rendition="#right">“<hi rendition="#small-caps">Royal
                                Commission Jamaica</hi>,<lb/>“<hi rendition="#small-caps">King’s
                                House, Spanish Town</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 15,
                            1866.</p>
                        <p rendition="#flush">“To Lieutenant-General <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Salomon</hi>,<lb/>“<hi rendition="#italic">Ex-Senator and Secretary
                                of State of the Republic of Hayti</hi>:</p>
                        <p>“<hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                            the receipt, &amp;c.</p>
                        <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                        <p>“Permit me to say to your excellency that since His Excellency Governor
                            Eyre has, in justification of the order of your arrest and your
                            expulsion then from this island, given as reason, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">that you were a supposed</hi> accomplice of
                            designs against the Government of Hayti, with which republic Her Majesty
                            is in friendly relation, it is evident that your case is not within the
                            limit of the inquiries with which the commission of Her Majesty finds
                            itself charged.</p>
                        <p>“I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">“CHARLES C. ROUNDELL,<lb/>“<hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Secretary of the Royal Commission.</hi>”</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">“<hi rendition="#small-caps">British Legation</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Port-au-Prince, January</hi> 20,
                        1872.</p></quote></p>
                <p><quote rend="blockquote"><p rendition="#flush">“To Messrs. <hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Cheesman, J. J. Riviere, F. Herman</hi>, and
                                <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. F. Martineau</hi>:</p>
                        <p>“<hi rendition="#small-caps">Sirs</hi>: I have the honor, &amp;c.* * *
                            Every government <hi rendition="#italic">has the right to expel</hi> a
                            foreigner from its territory <hi rendition="#italic">if it suspects
                                him</hi> to conspire against it or against a neighboring or friendly
                            government. It was for this reason that order was given to General
                            Salomon to quit Jamaica.</p>
                        <p>“I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">“SPENCER ST. JOHN,<lb/>“<hi rendition="#italic">Her
                                Britannic Majesty’s Chargé d’Ajfairs.</hi>”</p></quote></p>
